-----BEGIN PGP SIGNED MESSAGE-----

Attention Linux Users in the Duke University Community !!!

For those of you who do not know, there is a very active Linux
Users' Group at NC State University. Last year these guys put
together a Linux Expo that highlighted a number of good talks
on various aspects of Linux use and development. 

This year ... the Linux Expo is back !!! 

It will be held on Centennial Campus at NCSU (in Raleigh, NC)
on April 13, 1996. It is sponsored by the kind folks at 
RedHat Software.

Key features --

  There will be an entire day of "scheduled talks on the best 
  and greatest of Linux". 

  Demos of what Linux can do including a Digital Alpha running 
  Linux from Red Hat Software.

  Good Linux info as seen last year ...

  A number of vendors demonstrating their products...


The cost of this expo is 2 bucks (yes, that's all) for _all_
students IF you _preregister_. It is 4 bucks at the door (still
a bargain). 

Check out the NCSU LUG page for more info at
http://www.linux.ncsu.edu


Anyone who has been to any sort of conference or users' group
meeting knows that a big chunk of the benefits from going come
from OTHER ATTENDEES. Attendance is what really makes these 
things tick so please try to attend. I am sure there will be 
something for Linux users of all levels. 

For the Duke people who are interested in going, please send me
an email if you need directions (I got my BS and MS at NCSU).

If you need or can provide a ride let me know ... I will do what
I can. 
 
