i have uploaded version 0.7 of dxpc to:
     ftp://sunsite.unc.edu/pub/Linux/Incoming/dxpc-0.7.tar.gz

it will soon move to:
     ftp://sunsite.unc.edu/pub/Linux/X11/xutils/dxpc-0.7.tar.gz


dxpc is a "Differential X Protocol Compressor" that compresses
the X protocol for improved performance over low-bandwidth
network connections.

from the README:

> 0. WHAT'S NEW IN THIS RELEASE
>    ==========================
> 
> The new command-line option "-u" can be used to keep dxpc_client
> from creating a UNIX domain socket.  (I.e., if the "-u" option is
> used, dxpc will listen only on a TCP port, not on a UNIX domain
> socket.)  This may be useful on systems where dxpc_client does not
> have write permission for /tmp/.X11-unix.
> 
> The new command-line options "-s1" and "-s2" cause dxpc to print
> information about its compression performance when an X client
> terminates.
> 
> dxpc version 0.7 provides slightly better compression than
> version 0.6.


