-----BEGIN PGP SIGNED MESSAGE-----

This is a release of the U-Net low-latency, user-level communication 
system developed by the the Systems Group at the Cornell University
Computer Science Department. 

U-Net is a network interface for protected, user-level communication over
ATM and Fast Ethernet. It provides low-latency and high-bandwidth I/O for
parallel and distributed computation on workstation clusters and similar
systems. Round-trip message latency has been measured at 60 usec (Fast
Ethernet) and 65 usec (ATM) for 40-byte messages.

This system has been described in the SOSP '95 paper "U-Net: A User-Level
Network Interface for Parallel and Distributed Computing", by A. Basu et. al.

This is release 2.0, dated 10-March-1996. This is a PRELIMINARY RELEASE;
a number of features are unsupported, but are currently underway. 
Expect a 2.1 release soon.

This distribution currently supports the following platforms:
	FORE Systems SBA-200 ATM under SunOS 4.1.x and Solaris 2.x
	FORE Systems PCA-200 ATM under Linux 1.3.x.
	DECChip 21140 ("Tulip") PCI Fast Ethernet under Linux 1.3.x.	

The software is available from
	ftp://ftp.cs.cornell.edu/pub/mdw/unet/unet-2.tar.gz

Documentation, papers, notes, etc. are available at
	http://www.cs.cornell.edu/Info/Projects/U-Net/

If you download and plan to use this software, please drop a note to
Matt Welsh (mdw@cs.cornell.edu). I will be creating a low-traffic mailing
list for U-Net users to keep everyone informed of updates and fixes.

Feel free to get in touch with the Cornell U-Net group for bug reports,
suggestions, problems, and general support. We would like to hear from you!

Best of luck!

Matt Welsh (mdw@cs.cornell.edu)
Thorsten von Eicken (tve@cs.cornell.edu)

