CLUE Newsletter, March 1996
===========================

The Colorado Linux Users & Enthusiasts (CLUE), normally meets the
    third Thursday of every month. The next meeting will be at
    7:00pm on March 21st. The location will be Smoky Hill High
    School, located at 16100 E. Smoky Hill Rd. in Southeast
    Aurora.
    
CLUE has a home page!  Find us at http://spot.elfwerks.com/~clue/
    Mike Miller is the Webmaster for our pages.
    
Library Reminder: Please bring unneeded Linux CD distributions
    and other Linux items that help "share Linux with the world"
    to the next CLUE meeting for the Linux Library!

CLUE is for anyone with an interest in Linux, whether you are an
    expert, or just interested and want to know more about the
    Internet and Operating System phenomena that Linux
    represents. All interested parties are invited to attend.
    Let's learn from each other!

For more information, or to be added/removed from the CLUE
    mailing list contact Joel at 303-784-2795 or E-Mail:
    joel@mrg.uswest.com, or attend a meeting, and turn in your
    information there. There is no cost for membership or
    newsletter subscription via E-Mail. 
    
Future Meeting dates will be: 
    April 18, May 16, June 20...
      (more dates to be announced - waiting for confirmation 
      of summer dates from SHHS.  Anticipate meetings on the
      3rd Thursday of each month)

Directions to Smoky Hill High School:  Take Parker south from
    I-225, to Quincy.  There will be a shopping center on the
    left, and a Stoplight. Take a left on Quincy. Then the first
    stoplight with a right turn will be Smoky Hill Road.  Turn
    right onto Smoky Hill, cross Chambers (a light), and then
    turn right at Laredo (a stop light), then left into the
    School parking lot. Go past the main entrance, and to the
    activities entrance.  There will be signs posted in the
    building to direct you to the room where we meet.

Vendors are encouraged to attend, make Linux-related
    announcements, etc. 
    
Questions and Information: joel@mrg.uswest.com


Topics:
    March News
    CLUE Linux CD/Book Library
    Presenters Needed
    Help Wanted/For Hire/Wanted/For Sale
    Administrivia/Credits


March News
- ----------
    Upcoming:
    
    At the March 21st regular meeting we are excited to have
    representatives from XInside - makers of the Accelerated X
    product and other tools - to join us to talk about
    their products, history with Linux, and outlook for the future. 
    Thanks to Lee Roder of XInside for coming to talk with us!
    We look forward to seeing you there!
    
    Past:
    
    In March we had our first "Event" - A Linux Install Day, held on
    Saturday, March 9th.  Eric Gustafson and Rich Maginn hosted the
    event at Smoky Hill High School.  Over 30 machines were brought
    in to have Linux installed for the first time, to get hardware
    trouble assistance, or to try out a new install.  Many of the
    machines were connected to the school network with ethernet for
    NFS-installs of Slackware or RedHat. While most every machine got
    up and running with Linux by the end of the day, not all the
    questions could be answered (Teac 4x CD-ROM connected to a
    SoundBlaster, anyone?)  Everyone went away a little more
    knowledgeable at the end of the day.  Rich Maginn called it "an
    incredible success."  Thanks to everyone who participated!

    At the February meeting we had representatives from
    Stonehenge Internet, a local (Denver) Internet provider which
    uses Linux for its primary servers. They spoke about the
    services they offer, and their experiences with Linux as an
    Internet WWW/News/Mail/etc. server.

