Thot, a document editor is available on Linux, as a free binary
distribution intended to academic institutions. A personnal use
is also allowed.

What is Thot:
- -------------

Thot is a structured document editor, presenting a graphical WYSIWYG
interface under X-Windows. It offers the usual functionality of a word
processor, but it also handles the document structure.

Thot uses the document structure to guide the user and to generate
automatically certain parts of documents. It also formats documents on
the basis of their structure and performs such operations as section
numbering or cross-references update.

Thot includes a set of advanced tools, specially a multilingual
spelling checker and an index generator.

Thot is an integrated and extensible system. It can process with the
same tool and within the same document not only structured text but
also graphics, complex tables, and mathematical formulae.

Thot is an open system. It is able to exchange documents with other
systems through a flexible exporting tool. For example, documents can
be converted into LaTeX or HTML.

 
How to download and to get more information:
- --------------------------------------------

Thot is developed by project Opera (INRIA-IMAG) in France.
To get more information on Thot and the team who developped it,
go to the following URL with your favorite WWW browser:

    http://opera.inrialpes.fr/thot/

A mailing list devoted to the support of Thot on Linux has been set up.
You can send messages to linux-thot@imag.fr . You can also subscribe by
sending a mail to majordomo@imag.fr containing the following line in the
body:

       subscribe linux-thot
       
The mailing list is also archived at the following URL:

    http://opera.inrialpes.fr/thot/messages/

Please read them before posting questions on the list.

  for the Opera team,

 linuxly yours,

Daniel

