                              Scilab-2.2

	Scilab Group is proud to announce the birth of Scilab-2.2. Faster
than before, stronger than before, leaner than before, Scilab can solve
all your numerical problems better than before. 

What is Scilab?
- ---------------
	Scilab is a high-level language for numerical computations in a 
user-friendly environment. Scilab is developed at INRIA and is available 
free via anonymous ftp in source and binary formats.

What is new
- ------------
   Too many changes to list here. Here are just a few highlights.

     - New solvers
	* Scicos: a hybrid dynamic system simulator using block 
            diagram description with a nice GUI (beta test).
        * A discrete/continuous ode solver odedc.
        * DAE solver with root finder (dasrt).

     - New GUI utilities
        * Choice menu for setting graphics parameters.
        * Menus to print and export graphics.
        * Mouse driven zoom for 2d plots and rotate for 3d plots.
        * Function to create and handle new buttons.

     - New Optimization routines
        * New versions of optimization routines.
        * Non differentiable optimization.

     - Revised version of the graph and network analysis toolbox Metanet.
    
     - Miscellaneous improvements
	* Easier installation with configure.
        * On-line resizing of Scilab stack [Dynamic allocation].
        * Read and write in integer format.
        * New data type "typed-list" for "soft coded" operations (tlist).
        * Function to kill graphic windows (xdel); possible also by menu.
	* Postscript documentations in a separate directory

     - Bugs corrected
         * A lot! And twice as many new ones introduced!

Distribution
- ------------
	As usual, Scilab is distributed free with the sources and runs on
most Unix-Xwindows system. Scilab can be otained by anonymous ftp from
"ftp.inria.fr:/INRIA/Scilab" (internet# 192.93.2.54).

	In this directory you will find scilab-2.2-src.tar.gz which is the
source version and two binary distributions scilab-2.2-Linux-a.out.tar.gz
and scilab-2.2-Linux-elf.tar.gz. There are of course binary versions
for many other Unix worksations (Sun, Dec, HP, ...).

Unlike previous releases, the postscript documentations are no longer
included in Scilab package, but are available in the subdirectory 
"Scilab-2.2-doc" (Latex sources though are included).

	In the subdirectory "contrib", you will find contributions made
by Scilab users. For the moment there is a port of Scilab 2.1
on the MacIntosh and soon there will be a few functions for reading and
writing images, a toolbox for Hidden Markov Models and more...

	For questions and suggestions write to Scilab@inria.fr

                                                     Doctor Scilab



