		    POSTIT - An NNTP client for posting
		    ===================================

			      Version 0.4
		       Written by Egil Kvaleberg
				    
				 ------

Postit is an NNTP client for UNIX. It will connect to a remote NNTP server
and post outgoing articles batched by the news system.

Together with Slurp, it will provide the NNTP capabilites required for
small news spools on installations with NNTP access only through limited
ISP accounts with dialup SLIP/PPP connection.

- - Compatible with Cnews. Should be easy to adapt for INN too.

- - Error recovery. In the event of an error occurring while articles are
  being posted, the message IDs of failed articles are maintained in 
  the spool file. 

- - No configuration required.

- - Logging to syslog of the number of succesfully posted, missing and
  duplicate articles at the end of a session plus, if required, the
  transfer speed of the article posting stage.

- - Executable is included. To recompile, copy of Slurp source is required.

Postit was written in C under Linux, and should be quite portable. File 
locking is handled by a shell script (Cnews style).

