   dir:   pub/vms/linux
   files: gv_2_3_b1.tar.gz

gv 2.3 is a port of GhostView-VMS 2.3 to Linux.
GhostView-VMS 2.3 is an X11 frontend to ghostscript, based on
Terry Poot's port of Tim Theisen's ghostview 1.5 to VMS.

This version is for beta testing only. It was created on
   Linux 1.2.13 i586  with X11R6
and up to now it is tested only within this environment.

Apart from further reduction of bugs this release also intends
to serve as the basis for exporting gv 2.3 to other Unix flavors.
Except of standard incompatibilities (header files etc.) such a
port shouldn't pose many problems.

Requirements:
- -------------

   o To install gv 2.3 you need the Xaw3d widget set including its
     header files.
     If you don't have the Xaw3d sources already you may obtain
     them via anonymous ftp from
        Linux version:
           site: sunsite.unc.edu
           dir:  /pub/Linux/distributions/debian/development/source/x11
           file: xaw3d-1.2a-1.tar.gz
           (this is the version I'm using on Slackware 3.0)
        Otherwise:
           site: ftp.x.org
           dir:  /contrib/widgets/Xaw3d

   o Ghostscript 2.6 or higher. To view PDF files with gv you
     will need at least ghostscript 3.51.
     You may obtain the latest version of ghostscript via 
     anonymous ftp from
         site:  ftp.cs.wisc.edu
         dir:   /ghost/aladdin


