This is an announcement of a test release of the OggSquish lossless/lossy audio
codec (version 0.97c).  At the moment, this is a UNIX only release (native
platform is Linux) of a command line encoder/decoder, but we'll have a real
encode/decode/play application with nice friendly buttons RSN :-)  DOS/Win/Mac
will follow soon.

This release is intended for very high quality compression, storage and
transmission of CD and similar quality audio.  It is not freeware, but it is 
completely free for all non-commercial and personal use; now you can put CD 
quality samples on your web pages to release all that yucky mulaw stuff! (We've 
applied for status as an official MIME encoding format).  OggSquish can happily
do realtime compression playback on 486/Pentium grade machines.

Please note also that the Web homepage for OggSQUISH moved about a year ago, and
lots of you out there who discovered it before then still have stale links.  The
current URL is http://deskfish.cs.titech.ac.jp:8001/squish/

The perceptual (MPEG-like) lossy modes are not in this release series yet, but
will be back soon.  It does include full lossless and fast (realtime, time-domain
only) lossy modes.

Binaries and source code are available at the above web site.  Further inquiries
should be directed to xiphmont@mit.edu

Have fun!  

Monty


