We are announcing the first Beta release of CERES Soundstudio for 
Linux. It'a multi-track wave file recorder, player and editor.

The software is provided "AS IS".

When you are using Ceres Soundstudio please send an E-Mail to 
100322.215@compuserve.com. The sole purpose of this is to
get an "use counter" and see, if the "linuxer's" like it or not.
Please feel free to make any suggestions or send in comments
regarding the Soundstudio.

This BETA version expires on July, 1st 1996. This day the release
version 1.0 will be shipped.


Download:
- ---------

You can download it via ftp from:

  sunsite.unc.edu /pub/Linux/Incoming/soundstudio.beta1.tgz


System requirements:
- --------------------

You need an ELF based Linux system. Soundstudio is a OSF/Motif 
application. It is statically linked with the Motif library
and dynamically linked with all the other freely available libraries.
For a proper execution of Ceres Soundstudio you need:

    * kernel with sound support (Voxware/TASD 2.9 or newer)
    * ld.so.1.7.14
    * libc.so.5.2.18
    * libm.so.5.0.5
    * libstdc++.so.27.1.0
    * XFree86 3.1.2
    * XPM Library

Newer versions of these components should work.
Using older versions is not recommended and not tested.


