Important notice for CDROM-distribution producers:


Changes have taken place in the interfacing to some CDROM drives with
a proprietary interface, especially for software configurable
interface cards.  At this moment these changes concern the cdrom
interface on the ISP16/MAD16/Mozart sound cards and therefore also the
drives of the types Optics Storage DOLPHIN 8000AT and Sanyo CDR-H94A
and any other CDROM driver which includes detection and/or
configuration code for a cdrom interface.

The Linux drivers optcd and sjcd for the drives mentioned contained
code for autodetecting and enabling the software configurable cdrom
interface part of ISP16/MAD16/Mozart sound cards.  Detection and
configuration of CDROM interfaces preferably should be kept out of
CDROM drivers, as has been done with optcd and sjcd drivers as of
kernel 1.3.63. This separation of the interface-configuration code
from the driver was set up to be able to support any combination of
cdrom interface and cdrom drive.  The detection ans configuration code
can be enabled by saying Y to the kernel configuration questions 'Soft
configurable cdrom interface card support' and 'ISP16/MAD16/Mozart
soft configurable cdrom interface support'. Extension and support for
other cards is forthcoming.  If you have any ideas for more support,
please contact us.  For more information, please read
Documentation/cdrom/isp16.

Distribution providers: please enable this code in your installation
kernels!  This is _essential_ for the people using any CDROM drive
connected to a supported interface card, to be able to install from
CDROM.

The soft configurable cdrom interface support code for
ISP16/MAD16/Mozart cards by default configures these for the Sanyo
CDR-H94A drive, base address 0x340, no irq/dma drive.  This base
address and irq/dma are also the defaults of the optcd and sjcd
drivers. Any of these can be set by the LILO command-line option
starting with "isp16=".  People using an Optics Storage drive should
override the default with the command-line option "isp16=Sony".
(Optics Storage uses the Sony proprietary interface.)

Please point this out to the users of your CDROM distribution, e.g.,
by quoting the previous paragraph in your manual.


Please direct comments and questions to:

Eric van der Maarel <H.T.M.v.d.Maarel@marin.nl>
Leo Spiekman <spiekman@et.tudelft.nl>



