Version 1.2.6 of the KBackup backup system for UNIX has 
been released.

CHANGES:

This version is mainly a maintenance release, with some improvements
and bug fixes added to 1.2.5. Also the manual has been updated.

If you are running a version older than 1.2.5 you should upgrade.
The next major release 1.3.0 will be in about a month or so.

                             WHERE?

KBackup has been uploaded to
ftp://sunsite.unc.edu/pub/Linux/Incoming/KBackup-1.2.6.tar.gz
and will soon appear at:
ftp://sunsite.unc.edu/pub/Linux/system/Backup/KBackup-1.2.6.tar.gz

It is also available from:
ftp://ftp.rz.uni-karlsruhe.de/pub/linux/local/soft/KBackup-1.2.6.tar.gz

For more details see the KBackup Homepage, including a hypertext version
of the complete manual:
http://www.uni-karlsruhe.de/~Karsten.Ballueder



                              WHAT?

KBackup is a powerful yet user-friendy backup system.

Among the many features included are:
  - support for tapes, floppies and removable hard disks
  - really user-friendly menu-controlled operation
  - afio or tar format 
  - optional software compression and double buffering
  - automatic handling of multi-volume archives, 
    detects end of tape
  - quick archive directory access
  - automatic detection of archive format and option settings
  - optional public key encryption using pgp(1)
  - support for high capacity floppy formats
  - scheduled operation at a later time or regularly
  - full or incremental backups
  - extensive manual and documentation
  - high portability to other platforms
  - automatic detection of the right tape device to use
  - ....many many more

