I have uploaded two real time spectrum analysis programs to
sunsite.unc.edu.  These programs record audio data from a sound card,
perform an FFT, and plot the results in either a frequency-amplitude plot
(freq51.tar.gz) or a time-frequency-amplitude plot (specgrm2.tar.gz).  The
graphics display is done using either the SVGALib package (for full-screen
display) or the SRGP package (for X-Windows display), which must be
obtained and installed separately.  The included executables are
dynamically linked with ELF versions of the libraries.

The programs are currently in /pub/Linux/Incoming, but will eventually be 
moved to /pub/Linux/apps/sound/freqs.  The source for these programs 
(included) can also be compiled in DOS for use with SB16, PAS16, and SB8 
soundcards.

