Hello,

	Following is to note current status of directories
	at  ftp.funet.fi  (aka nic.funet.fi), and related
	things here.

	First of all, we try to refer this cluster of machines
	with service oriented names, thus we prefer:

		ftp.funet.fi

	instead of the generic cluster name:  nic.funet.fi
	(See at page   http://www.funet.fi/index-en.html  at
	 "servers, and services" for what we mean with 'cluster')

	Paths within this server have evolved over the years,
	and for a couple of years now, our Linux material has
	been at directory:  /pub/Linux/   while the original
	/pub/OS/Linux/  is symbolic link to the real place.

	It is however, a bit annoying to note, that still quite
	a large part of traffic goes via /pub/OS/Linux/ -path,
	causing Linux to be second to msdos at our top-traffic
	statistics... A snapshot from yesterday's report:

	                                        ---- Percent  of ----
	Archive section Bytes sent  Files sent  Bytes sent Files sent
	--------------- ---------- ----------- ---------- ----------
	msdos           3856625400       16157     23.41 %    14.44 %
	Linux           3753403640       22147     22.78 %    19.80 %
	OS              1154361215        9424      7.01 %     8.43 %

	I leave it as an excercise for you to calculate, what is
	our 24h average of kilobytes per second via FTP...  :-)



	To summarize:

	Preferred reference:

		ftp://ftp.funet.fi/pub/Linux/

	Depreciated:

		ftp://nic.funet.fi/pub/Linux/
		ftp://nic.funet.fi/pub/OS/Linux/
		ftp://ftp.funet.fi/pub/OS/Linux/


/Matti Aarnio <mea@nic.funet.fi>  Of "managers" -group

	Linux archive correspondence:  <linux-adm@nic.funet.fi>
	Overall FTP-server questions:  <problems@nic.funet.fi>
	Supervising administrators:    <managers@nic.funet.fi>


