From: alaric@babcom.com (The Renaissance Man)
Subject: PATCH: Spam patch for suck-2.6.1
Date: 1996/03/20
Message-ID: <cola-liw-827358084-10592-1@oravannahka.helsinki.fi>#1/1
X-Deja-AN: 143222856
x-original-date: 16 Mar 1996 17:49:43 -0800
followup-to: comp.os.linux.networking
content-type: text/plain; charset=ISO-8859-1
organization: The Babylon Project
mime-version: 1.0
newsgroups: comp.os.linux.announce

-----BEGIN PGP SIGNED MESSAGE-----


The following batch for Bob Yetman's very useful SUCK package adds the
ability to automatically kill articles crossposted to more than N groups,
by adding the command "SPAM=N" to your suck.killfile, where N is the maximum 
number of groups you want to allow articles to be crossposted to.


For example, if your suck.killfile contains the line:

SPAM=10

then any article posted to 11 or more newsgroups will be killed.


I have taken the liberty of tagging this, for my site, as suck-2.6.2. 
This patch is from suck-2.6.1.  The only files changed are killfile.c and
killfile.h.  I have not yet updated suck.1 to reflect these changes. 




diff -Bd suck-2.6.1/killfile.c suck-2.6.2/killfile.c
43c43,44
< 	"Multiple Matches/Tiebreaker Used"
- ---
> 	"Multiple Matches/Tiebreaker Used",
> 	"Excessive Crossposting"
46c47
< REASON_SUBJECT, REASON_FROM, REASON_NOKEEP, REASON_TIE};
- ---
> REASON_SUBJECT, REASON_FROM, REASON_NOKEEP, REASON_TIE, REASON_SPAM};
61c62,63
< 	{6, "QUOTE=", 0, ""}
- ---
> 	{6, "QUOTE=", 0, ""},
> 	{5, "SPAM=", 12, "Newsgroups: " }
63c65
< enum { PARAM_HILINE, PARAM_LOWLINE, PARAM_PATH, PARAM_SUBJ, PARAM_FROM, PARAM_GROUP, PARAM_QUOTE};
- ---
> enum { PARAM_HILINE, PARAM_LOWLINE, PARAM_PATH, PARAM_SUBJ, PARAM_FROM, PARAM_GROUP, PARAM_QUOTE, PARAM_SPAM};
465c467
< 			fprintf(fptr, "MESSAGE KILLED: %s - %s\n%s\n", group, Reasons[why], headerbuf);
- ---
> 			fprintf(fptr, "MESSAGE KILLED: %s - %s\n", group, Reasons[why]);
476c478
< 	char *startline;
- ---
> 	char *startline, *endline, *comma;
509a512,533
> 	/* check for spam */
> 	if(match == FALSE && killp->spam > 0) { 
> 		if((startline = strstr(headerbuf, Params[PARAM_SPAM].header)) != NULL)  {
> 			i = 1;	/* just in case */
> 			endline = strchr(startline, '\n');
> 			comma = NULL;  /* just in case */
> 			while ((comma = strchr(startline, ',')) != NULL)
> 			  {
> 			    startline = ++comma;
> 			    i++;
> 			  }
> #ifdef DEBUG2
> 			do_debug("Msg crossposted to %d newsgroups, max = %d\n", i, killp->spam);
> #endif
> 			if(i > killp->spam) {
> 				/* JACKPOT */
> 				match = TRUE;
> 				*why = REASON_SPAM;
> 			}
> 		}
> 		
> 	}
621c645
< 	mykill->hilines = mykill->lowlines = 0;
- ---
> 	mykill->hilines = mykill->lowlines = mykill->spam = 0;
695a720,725
> 						break;
> 					  case PARAM_SPAM:
> 						sscanf(&buf[Params[PARAM_SPAM].len], "%d", &(mykill->spam));
> #ifdef DEBUG2
> 						do_debug("Killfile max crossposts = %d\n", mykill->spam);
> #endif
diff -Bd suck-2.6.1/killfile.h suck-2.6.2/killfile.h
8a9
> 	int spam;       /* max nr of groups on newsgroups line */




Enjoy.



